 {"$schema":"fabro-journal-v1","run_id":"01M25R832HP615J291N72FHNCS","node":"planner","visit":1,"status":"succeeded","ts":"2026-09-10T13:33:46Z","data":{"painpoints":[{"text":"fabro_runs_list reports PR #121 as state 'merged' while the base branch has none of its work (no lifecycle_events.rs, no squash commit; newest base commit 76ed619 explicitly says the close lives only on the unmerged branch). The in-flight check relies on run/PR projections — a wrongly-'merged' open PR is invisible as in-flight and misleads reconciliation. Evidence: runs list for workflow develop, run 01M25K41V4NEWXSA3SVGRHKRXK, checked 2026-09-10 in run 01M25R832HP615J291N72FHNCS. Fix idea: postlude/post-merge reconciliation should correct PR state, or the projection should re-check against git."},{"text":"Journal fallback for run 01M23RQRCB748R4VRXA2WE6BZ0 (open PR #109) found no journal file at `.fabro/journal/<run_id>.jsonl` — had to recover the in-flight seed (fabro-e702) by fetching the run branch and parsing the .seeds/issues.jsonl diff. This is exactly the known gap of seed fabro-adf7 (failed runs lose stage journals); the prompt's journal fallback silently degrades to nothing."}],"observations":["In-flight exclusions applied this pass: fabro-e702 (open PR #109, seed recovered via run-branch seeds diff), and self (this run). PR #109 is old (2026-09-09) and still open — a stale in-flight lock on its seed.","fabro-3fe4 re-claimed rather than fabro-7627 (also High, listed first): tie-break per observed-failure-class rule — 3fe4 has a concrete gate failure and ~55 min of reusable work on the PR #121 branch; 7627 stays top of the next run's list.","The runs-list 'merged' state for PR #121 contradicts base history; the seed's REOPEN CONTEXT (base commit 76ed619) was treated as authoritative. The implementer MUST fetch the PR #121 branch before starting."]}}
+{"$schema":"fabro-journal-v1","run_id":"01M25R832HP615J291N72FHNCS","node":"implementer","visit":1,"status":"succeeded","ts":"2026-09-10T14:54:35Z","data":{"painpoints":[{"text":"The reopen brief's git fetch of `fabro/run/01M25K41V4NEWXSA3SVGRHKRXK` produced branch commits (7a0a7db, f051098) whose fixes were partially superseded by an in-progress unstaged worktree state with no journal record explaining it — an interrupted prior pass of run 01M25R832HP left ambiguous reconciliation state. Suggestion: journal the reconciliation decision (reuse vs supersede) as the first action of a re-claim pass so the next interruption is recoverable."}],"observations":["The PR #121 branch's fix (Runnable-retry inside the Rejected arm + durable-terminal fallback in the delete guard) diverged from the worktree's cleaner shared-helper fix; choosing the shared helper required reading both diffs carefully — the branch's zz_probe_seeded_completed_status debug test in `lib/apps/fabro-cli/tests/it/cmd/rm.rs` is correctly absent from the final tree.","rg pattern `pub fn` misses `pub async fn` declarations — lifecycle_events.rs looked empty on first inventory; pattern discipline matters when verifying module interfaces."]}}
